00:01:26,095 --> 00:01:29,047
It's not some HTML code sent by a server,

34
00:01:29,127 --> 00:01:31,515
instead it's written in the code with which

35
00:01:31,628 --> 00:01:32,637
the app was written.

36
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:35,041
And you can build something similar on the

37
00:01:35,073 --> 00:01:37,125
web with a single page application.

38
00:01:37,782 --> 00:01:40,859
That's an application where a single HTML

39
00:01:40,939 --> 00:01:42,991
file is requested from a server,

40
00:01:43,552 --> 00:01:45,315
and that could be a different server than

41
00:01:45,395 --> 00:01:46,853
your API server, by the way.

42
00:01:47,639 --> 00:01:50,636
And that single HTML page includes a bunch

43
00:01:50,636 --> 00:01:52,799
of JavaScript code, typically

44
00:01:53,504 --> 00:01:56,918
using one of the popular frontend JavaScript

45
00:01:56,934 --> 00:01:59,676
frameworks, Angular, React, and Vue would be

46
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:00,478
the big ones there.

47
00:02:01,103 --> 00:02:02,803
And thereafter, it's that browser-side

48
00:02:02,803 --> 00:02:05,289
JavaScript code that is responsible for

49
00:02:05,289 --> 00:02:07,486
bringing something onto the screen, for

50
00:02:07,534 --> 00:02:09,105
rendering something onto the screen.

51
00:02:09,843 --> 00:02:12,104
Now, no matter if you're working with a

52
00:02:12,104 --> 00:02:14,365
frontend that's a mobile app or if it's a

53
00:02:14,365 --> 00:02:15,921
single-page web application,

54
00:02:16,739 --> 00:02:17,204
either way,

55
00:02:17,781 --> 00:02:21,646
those apps don't want HTML code because they

56
00:02:21,726 --> 00:02:23,634
already know how to bring something on the

57
00:02:23,634 --> 00:02:26,670
screen. Instead, they just want data to

58
00:02:26,767 --> 00:02:29,980
populate their screens with the actual data.

59
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:33,114
And therefore, they will send requests to

60
00:02:33,194 --> 00:02:36,183
your API server requesting certain data, for

61
00:02:36,183 --> 00:02:38,577
example, a list of products, let's say.

62
00:02:39,381 --> 00:02:41,566
Now, your server might then reach out to a

63
00:02:41,566 --> 00:02:44,587
database or to the file system depending on

64
00:02:44,699 --> 00:02:46,820
what it needs to do. It will then fetch and

65
00:02:46,933 --> 00:02:50,114
prepare that data or maybe store data if the

66
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:52,186
the frontend app sent some data that should

67
00:02:52,250 --> 00:02:52,668
be stored.

68
00:02:53,294 --> 00:02:55,526
And whenever the server is done, it will

69
00:02:55,767 --> 00:02:59,942
respond back with data in that JSON format.

70
00:03:00,296 --> 00:03:02,785
So it will send back data. It will never

71
00:03:02,785 --> 00:03:06,141
send back HTML code. It will never send back

72
00:03:06,221 --> 00:03:08,534
what should be rendered on the screen. It

73
00:03:08,614 --> 00:03:11,633
only sends back data and it's then up to the

74
00:03:11,681 --> 00:03:14,572
frontend app to decide what to do with that

75
00:03:14,572 --> 00:03:17,013
data and what to draw onto the screen.

76
00:03:18,425 --> 00:03:21,923
Therefore, in the API case, our API server

77
00:03:22,052 --> 00:03:24,651
simply provides multiple so-called

78
00:03:24,908 --> 00:03:28,823
endpoints, which are URL HTTP method

79
00:03:28,855 --> 00:03:29,626
combinations,

80
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:32,931
something like a POST request being sent to

81
00:03:33,268 --> 00:03:36,269
/products or a GET request being sent to

82
00:03:37,216 --> 00:03:37,793
/my-account.

83
00:03:38,563 --> 00:03:40,473
That would be an endpoint or that would be

84
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:43,618
endpoints and such endpoints are provided by

85
00:03:43,618 --> 00:03:46,315
the API server. And depending on which

86
00:03:46,572 --> 00:03:49,558
endpoint received a request, something will

87
00:03:49,622 --> 00:03:51,902
be done. For example, data will be stored in

88
00:03:51,902 --> 00:03:53,974
a database, data will be fetched from a

89
00:03:53,974 --> 00:03:57,153
database, and then that data will be sent

90
00:03:57,185 --> 00:04:01,215
back in JSON format to the standalone app,

91
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:04,378
which in the API server case is required

92
00:04:04,811 --> 00:04:08,119
because such an API server only replies with

93
00:04:08,247 --> 00:04:11,329
data, not with HTML. So not with

94
00:04:11,329 --> 00:04:13,878
instructions on what or how to render the

95
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:16,346
screen, just with the data. That's the

96
00:04:16,346 --> 00:04:17,180
important thing here.

97
00:04:17,709 --> 00:04:20,530
And a huge amount of web applications out

98
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:23,784
there are driven by such API servers. And in

99
00:04:23,816 --> 00:04:26,670
the end, any mobile app which you're using

100
00:04:27,006 --> 00:04:29,924
will talk to such an API server behind the

101
00:04:29,924 --> 00:04:33,018
scenes because it's a mobile app. Those apps

102
00:04:33,018 --> 00:04:34,284
have no chance of

103
00:04:35,038 --> 00:04:37,538
