106
00:04:42,331 --> 00:04:45,265
apps. So therefore, API servers are an

107
00:04:45,314 --> 00:04:47,462
important building block of the modern web,

108
00:04:47,863 --> 00:04:49,980
and therefore we'll have an entire section

109
00:04:50,012 --> 00:04:52,705
in this course on how to build a REST API,

110
00:04:53,218 --> 00:04:55,575
which is just the most popular form of an

111
00:04:55,575 --> 00:04:56,361
API server.

112
00:04:57,003 --> 00:04:59,247
But we also have that other approach, which

113
00:04:59,247 --> 00:05:01,572
is also very important, and that would be a

114
00:05:01,572 --> 00:05:04,346
server returning server-side rendered views.

115
00:05:05,276 --> 00:05:07,874
If we compare it to the API server, the

116
00:05:07,970 --> 00:05:11,498
difference is that for the server-side

117
00:05:11,498 --> 00:05:13,023
rendered views server,

118
00:05:13,682 --> 00:05:16,635
we don't have frontend apps. Instead, we

119
00:05:16,635 --> 00:05:19,171
just have our client, so the user using a

120
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:21,756
